# Hot/Cold ClickBench-100M recency-boundary tuples (D-HC-0403 amended; see METHODOLOGY-LOG L0034).
# Split key = the UNIQUE 5-tuple (EventTime, WatchID, UserID, CounterID, EventDate) over the
# 99,997,497 rows of clickbench.hits_100m (uniqueness PROVEN: uniqExact == count).
# Recency order = (EventTime DESC, WatchID DESC, UserID DESC, CounterID DESC, EventDate DESC).
# hot(f)  = tuple >= B(f)  (the N(f) most-recent rows)   cold(f) = tuple < B(f)
# Each boundary B(f) is the N(f)-th most-recent row; counts verified EXACT (hot==N, hot+cold==total).
TOTAL_ROWS=99997497

# f = 1%  (N = 1,000,000)   hot=1,000,000  cold=98,997,497  EXACT
